// S175 Scenario A: exhaustion collapse cascade.
//
// Purpose: one critically tired agent rough-sleeps in the open while a hostile
// agent is permanently co-located. Every Sleep attempt is interrupted via
// SleepFailureCause::HostileProximity (an active sleep with a live, co-located
// hostile target is aborted with DangerNearby -> HostileProximity), and rough
// sleep recovers nothing (rough_sleep_recovery_floor: 0). Fatigue stays pinned
// at the authored critical value, fatigue_critical_ticks accumulates, and the
// S175 consequence path creates Exhaustion deprivation wounds. The first wound
// (severity 700, load 700) is below the 950 wound capacity; the second interval
// worsens the same wound to the Permille ceiling (1000 >= 950) and the agent
// dies from wound load attributed to Fatigue.
//
// The hostile "Watcher" is Human-controlled and never commanded, so it never
// attacks: the only consequence it produces is the per-tick hostile-proximity
// sleep interruption. Death is therefore an exhaustion collapse, not combat.
(
    seed: 175001,
    compaction_interval: 0,
    places: [
        (
            name: "Wilds",
            tags: [Camp],
        ),
    ],
    hostilities: [
        (subject: "Aster", target: "Watcher"),
        (subject: "Watcher", target: "Aster"),
    ],
    agents: [
        (
            name: "Aster",
            location: "Wilds",
